body:
@annevk 

If we can include  normative accessibility mappings in the HTML Standard can we also fork Web Speech API to HTML Standard? There is a relationship between accessibility mappings and Web Speech API in that we can, for example, convert Braille to audio, and audio to Braille, etc.; see https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2823.

While HTML Standard can make efforts to stay up to date with W3 version, will W3 also remain up to date with any changes made at HTML Standard version relevant to accessibility?

//cc @domenic

@domenic 

